# Line endings are a property of the REPO, so every clone gets them - not a
# setting each consumer has to rediscover.
#
# Git for Windows defaults core.autocrlf=true. Without this file a Windows clone
# lands as CRLF, and then ShellCheck rejects every shell file with SC1017
# ("Literal carriage return"): bin/fm-lint.sh fails on line 1 of everything and
# reports nothing at all about the code, and behavior assertions compare against
# strings that silently grew a \r. This repo is published for other Windows users
# to clone, and that first run is exactly the experience the Windows port exists
# to prevent.
#
# .github/workflows/windows-ci.yml also pins core.autocrlf=false and core.eol=lf
# before checkout. That stays as belt-and-braces; this file is the owner.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Pinned explicitly rather than left to text=auto's content sniffing, because a
# misdetected binary is a corrupted binary. assets/banner.png is the only
# non-text blob tracked here.
*.png binary
